{# IntelEngine tales, the chat form of decisions/intel_tale_turn.prompt: used when the player has no decision provider
   set up in SkyrimNet. Same context (npc_name, player_name, goal, transcript, outcomes, allow_none) and the same
   answer keys. #}
[ system ]
You read one conversation in a Skyrim story and say which prepared outcome it came to. Answer with ONLY a JSON object, nothing else.

[ user ]
{% if decision %}{{ player_name }} has a decision to make in front of {{ npc_name }}: {{ goal }}
{% else %}{{ player_name }} has been talking with {{ npc_name }}. What {{ player_name }} set out to do: {{ goal }}
{% endif %}

{{ transcript }}

{% if decision %}Has {{ player_name }} already told {{ npc_name }} their decision, in their own words? Name the answer that says the same as what {{ player_name }} actually said to {{ npc_name }}. Only {{ player_name }}'s own lines count, and only a plain statement of it: a question, a hint, a greeting, or words about something else is no decision, and then the answer is none.
{% else %}Going only by what was actually said, which of these outcomes has the conversation come to? An outcome about {{ npc_name }} has happened only when {{ npc_name }}'s own lines say it: what {{ player_name }} claims, asks or already knows is not {{ npc_name }}'s answer, and neither is a greeting, a gesture or talk about something else.
{% endif %}{% for o in outcomes %}
- {{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% if allow_none %}- none: none of these has happened yet
{% else %}Name the outcome closest to where the conversation ended; "none" is not allowed.
{% endif %}

Answer exactly like {{ "{" }}"turn":"o0"}
